So, NGAG.

00:14:29.639 --> 00:14:30.923
Then he says BSKYOD PA.

00:14:30.923 --> 00:14:34.262
You understand. MI BSKYOD PA - Akshobhya

00:14:35.289 --> 00:14:36.340
[Lady] Unshakable.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.780
Yes, steadfast as a mountain.

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.689
What is kshobhya?

00:14:40.689 --> 00:14:41.522
[Student's answer]

00:14:41.522 --> 00:14:42.861
What does it mean?

00:14:42.861 --> 00:14:46.120
[Student's answer]

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.832
Words and actions,

00:14:48.832 --> 00:14:49.940
physical behavior.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:54.940
This is interesting; he calls it movement.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.270
Move your body.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.912
How many kinds of karma are there so far?  Are both options

00:15:00.912 --> 00:15:02.195
good?  Two

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:10.293
Tim, $200 questions, from the two branches of Vidhamma

00:15:11.202 --> 00:15:15.202
RNAM RIG and RNAM RIG BYED MA YIN PA

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.810
... Think about the strange content related to karma in Chen Tang's text

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.819


00:15:24.819 --> 00:15:25.928
[Student's answer]

00:15:25.928 --> 00:15:30.928
No way!  $200!

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.780
Yes, firstly, what are some classic examples?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.130
When you take vows,

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.195
when you kneel down, your

00:15:36.195 --> 00:15:39.600
body holds a specific posture, and

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.590
anyone can guess your motives.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.040
That's MA KHYAB, right?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.369
You're probably thinking about lunch, but [laughs]

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:51.260
some people can guess your motives from your appearance.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.539
After that, according to Abhidharma, you'll have...?

00:15:55.539 --> 00:15:56.450
[Student's answer]

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.720
It's like a halo or aura surrounding you.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:03.070
That's the influence of the vows still lingering. It

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.630
's invisible.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:09.603
You can go to a bar, you can...

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:13.453
My translator in Mongolia was so cute.

00:16:13.453 --> 00:16:16.080
He said, "Geshe teacher, you've ruined my life!" The

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.500
second time I went there, he had a beard,

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.103
and then I said, "What happened?"

00:16:20.103 --> 00:16:24.430
He said, “Geshe, we’re
teaching Buddhism on national television.”

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.446
I said, “Okay,” and then he said,
“I can’t go to bars anymore.”

00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:29.760
[Laughter]

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.820
Everyone keeps asking, so I have to grow a beard

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.280
so they won’t recognize me.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:37.020
Why are we talking about this?

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:39.910
You wouldn't guess that the bearded man in the bar

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.680
has a karmic aura—the

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.043
karmic aura of someone teaching Buddhism on national television.

00:16:46.139 --> 00:16:47.550
NGAG DANG BSKYOD DANG

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.098
Okay, those two are RNAM RIG

00:16:49.098 --> 00:16:52.365
Tim. What is MA YIN DGAG?

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:57.353
If the first two are RNAM RIG…

00:16:57.353 --> 00:16:58.440
[Student answers]

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.558
Yes, then the next one will be

00:17:00.558 --> 00:17:02.480
RNAM RIG MA YIN,
a non-communicative aura (without color).

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.310
Now he's talking about auras.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:10.310
So far, there have been two, we have words and body language.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:15.270
Now we have RNAM RIG MIN.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:18.310
Then he calls it MI SPONG BA.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:23.160
You don't give up, don't give up. Lama

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.810
Chögyam Trung said that's Nagarjuna. It's a

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.417
shortened expression for MI DGE BA, which means don't give up.

00:17:31.111 --> 00:17:32.600
[Student answers]

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.933
Yes, so that means you are?

00:17:35.962 --> 00:17:39.812
If you are MI DGE BA SPONG, then who are you?

00:17:39.812 --> 00:17:42.807
If you give up MI DGE BA, what are you?

00:17:42.807 --> 00:17:44.370
DGE BA, yes.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:49.370
So why did Nagarjuna
call virtuous deeds "the act of not giving up"?

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:56.743
That's because you haven't given up on evil.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:01.170
He's describing good as not giving up,

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:04.350
but that means

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.453
not giving up on evil, that's good.

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:13.214
[Student response]

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.760
Sorry, give up on evil. Okay.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.194


00:18:18.194 --> 00:18:21.070
MI SPONG RNAM RIG MIN.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:24.303
I'm sorry, I messed up, let's try again.

00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:28.490
MI SPONG BA means, I'm sorry.

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:31.190
Yes, you don't give up on evil.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:34.180
I got it right the first time.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.634
What is it?

00:18:35.634 --> 00:18:38.173
[Woman] MI DGE BA
An evil deed

00:18:38.173 --> 00:18:39.310
[Student's answer]

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.140
No, not giving up evil deeds.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.240
Not giving up evil deeds is evil karma, that's it.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.073
Okay, understand?

00:18:45.073 --> 00:18:47.690
So the first one is correct.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.300
So, the third category

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:54.960
is not giving up evil deeds, which is evil karma.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.680
But we have already covered non-halo,

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:02.680
so this must be a halo,
meaning the peripheral light you receive. Lama

00:19:02.957 --> 00:19:06.100
Qiuni said... By the way,

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.508
this comes from Abhidharma.

00:19:07.508 --> 00:19:10.749
When you were engaged in trade in ancient India,

00:19:10.749 --> 00:19:15.683
you had to promise to do that profession.

00:19:16.816 --> 00:19:21.133
There are two famous vows
that people engaged in butchering and military service had to make:

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:24.820
I will shoot, I will kill.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:27.750
This is what is called @ What

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.644
is that?  A

00:19:29.644 --> 00:19:31.552
counter-oath is a broken oath.

00:19:31.552 --> 00:19:35.593
I pledged to follow my father's trade for the rest of my life.

00:19:35.593 --> 00:19:39.750
I have a friend in Argentina whose husband

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.380
slaughters animals in a factory.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:45.289
He's always frustrated, and they don't know why.

00:19:45.289 --> 00:19:46.560
[laughs] Okay,

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:51.120
so, we've talked about several kinds of karma so far?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:55.960
We talked about good karma, the karma of speech, and the

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.470
karma of actions you can see.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:02.010
Then we talked about bad karma, the halo, which is

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.300
making a promise.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:09.431
Now we have SPONG BA'I,

00:20:09.431 --> 00:20:12.597
which means you truly give up bad deeds.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:18.550
When you give up bad deeds, you will receive a halo. An

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.940
example of this halo is

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:24.910
when you are about to make a vow

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.862
to receive the Medicine Buddha empowerment, or

00:20:27.862 --> 00:20:29.100
when you receive the Bodhisattva vows.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.420
The halo shines on everyone in the class.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:36.100
If you participate in Nagarjuna's Bodhisattva vows ceremony,

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.210
you have a halo that will always surround you. Yes,

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:44.204
some people say that it stops when a person dies,

00:20:44.204 --> 00:20:47.450
but the halo of the Bodhisattva vows will not stop.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.700
So there are two kinds of halos: the

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:54.700
halo of good and bad, the halo of speech and the halo of actions, which
everyone can interpret.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:59.680
Then there are the halos of bad deeds and the halos of good deeds.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.890
We have four kinds now. How much has he promised us?

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.260
Seven kinds.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:05.060
He promised us seven kinds.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:09.094
Think about it, why did Master Nagarjuna arrange it this way?  Now that we've

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.611
reached the fifth type, how are you all doing?

00:21:12.611 --> 00:21:14.870
[Student's answer]

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.867
Yes, the non-communicative ones are three and four,

00:21:17.867 --> 00:21:20.490
while the communicative ones are one and two. Okay

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:21.323
, that's cool.

00:21:21.323 --> 00:21:25.865
We haven't entered the level of consciousness yet

00:21:25.865 --> 00:21:28.500
. LONGS SPYOD LAS BYUNG BSOD NAMS DANG,

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.513
GZHAN

00:21:32.781 --> 00:21:35.850
DAG KYANG NI DE BZHIN 'DOD' means

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.510
applying it to others.

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:42.613
And he means, good or bad.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.988
Okay?  Good or bad.

00:21:44.988 --> 00:21:48.530
When I categorize things as good or bad,

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:52.489
others continue to do so as well.

00:21:52.489 --> 00:21:56.200
LONGS SPYOD LAS BYUNG BSOD NAMS DANG.

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:58.080
This is interesting.

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:03.203
Material good deeds related to Buddhism.

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:06.670
Material good deeds related to Buddhism.

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:10.350
Donating with the Gold Club to protect ancient scriptures

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:15.280
or donating money to build a Medicine Buddha stupa.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.777
And in Abhidharma, there is a special name

00:22:17.777 --> 00:22:21.260
@.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:23.278
This is really interesting.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:29.860
I spent 30 years restoring a temple in New Jersey, a

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:32.210
Mongolian temple.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:37.080
I also rebuilt many houses, and so on.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:40.730
I still receive interest because of those actions.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.020
As long as there are monks living in those houses,

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.910
I have interest, karmic interest.

00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:46.530
This is called... @.

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:49.090
So what is the fifth one?

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:51.970
Nagarjuna believed it was

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:56.228
important to distinguish this special karma, that

00:22:56.228 --> 00:23:01.228
is, the material donations or contributions made for the Dharma,

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:05.910
because these contributions continue to flow after you leave. Even

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:10.300
after you leave the Golden Club, the
contributions you made continue to flow.

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:12.910
Suppose the Golden Club preserves many classical books;

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:16.360
then every time a Geshe teacher uses those books in class,

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:18.780
you still receive karmic interest.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:19.613
Pretty cool, right?

00:23:19.613 --> 00:23:21.030
For some reason, Nagarjuna believed that

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:23.503
distinguishing it is crucial.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.975
This could be the entire topic we discuss in a study group.

00:23:27.975 --> 00:23:30.880


00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:34.930
Okay, this means that projects like the Medicine Buddha Stupa
and the preservation of classical books

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.200
are interesting and "beneficial" projects

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:41.520
because you will always receive interest from them.

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:45.453
Even if you leave the group, you still benefit from it.

00:23:45.453 --> 00:23:47.110
Cool!

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:49.240
I'm still receiving interest.

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:51.940
I once built a water supply system at Sera Monastery,

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:53.680
and every time a monk drinks water,

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:56.650
I receive more karma.

00:23:56.650 --> 00:24:00.700
Okay, BSOD NAMS MA YIN TSUL DE BZHIN.

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:02.880
Conversely, Lama

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:05.770
Chögyam Truc said

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:09.060
an example is building a cattle slaughterhouse.

00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:11.990
If you build such a facility,
and they continue to slaughter cattle there,

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:13.770
you will continuously receive karmic interest.

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:15.630
This is the sixth one. We've finished talking about six.

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:18.695
What will the seventh one be?

00:24:18.695 --> 00:24:21.150
SEMS PA

00:24:21.150 --> 00:24:25.110
Pre-emptive Intention:

00:24:25.110 --> 00:24:28.100
What was your intention before you committed these six karmas?

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:31.060
What do you hope to gain?

00:24:31.060 --> 00:24:32.690
Good or bad,

00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:34.450
but he put them together, so that's seven.

00:24:34.450 --> 00:24:38.304
Therefore, we don't get the same number
because he put some together.

00:24:38.304 --> 00:24:40.850
Okay, LAS SU MNGON PAR 'DOD PA YIN.

00:24:40.850 --> 00:24:43.115
Some people really accept this.

00:24:43.115 --> 00:24:44.650
@

00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:45.483
Who is it?

00:24:45.483 --> 00:24:47.290
The Buddha

00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:50.620
described this as the first classification, which consisted of

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:53.488
only two types: SEMS PA and BSAM PA.

00:24:54.333 --> 00:24:57.865
Chetana and chetayitva.

00:24:57.865 --> 00:25:00.430
Now, there are seven types. Are

00:25:00.430 --> 00:25:02.430
there any more difficult verses so far?

00:25:03.725 --> 00:25:05.420
I think he'll come and lecture us soon.

00:25:05.420 --> 00:25:07.160
I think there will be a surprise.

00:25:07.160 --> 00:25:09.000
I'm just guessing.

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.690
There's a picture; try to find the images of these seven types.

00:25:12.690 --> 00:25:14.820
Good luck.

00:25:14.820 --> 00:25:18.054
I'm thinking about good karma and bad karma or something.

00:25:18.054 --> 00:25:19.340
I don't know.

00:25:19.340 --> 00:25:22.307
Anyway, let's continue.

00:25:25.644 --> 00:25:28.010
GAL TE SMIN PA'I DUS BAR DU

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:33.010
Now, finally, haha, he's set us up.

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:39.520
Why does he guide us with this calm, understandable
discussion about karma?

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:43.507
Because here it comes

00:25:43.507 --> 00:25:45.949
: GAL TE SMIN PA'I DUS BAR DU,

00:25:45.949 --> 00:25:48.341
,GNAS NA LAS DE RTAG PAR 'GYUR, ,

00:25:48.341 --> 00:25:52.416
GAL TE 'GAGS NA 'GAGS GYUR PA,

00:25:52.416 --> 00:25:54.420
,JI LTAR 'BRAS BU SKYE PAR 'GYUR,

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:57.220
Now, here's Nagarjuna's style:

00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:00.063
"Wow! We've created all sorts of karma.

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:03.710
So what happens next?"

00:26:03.710 --> 00:26:06.960
What do you think will happen next?

00:26:06.960 --> 00:26:10.053
Where does karma remain until it matures?

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.820
Now, he's set a trap for us with three verses, hasn't he?

00:26:15.820 --> 00:26:18.280
Section 5.

00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:19.980
He was setting a trap for us.

00:26:19.980 --> 00:26:22.610
Then he asked this naive question,

00:26:22.610 --> 00:26:27.610
"Oh, where does karma remain until it matures?"

00:26:27.680 --> 00:26:31.203
Then he said there are two possibilities:

00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:37.900
If it remains in an ineffective state until it manifests,

00:26:39.710 --> 00:26:40.850
then it is RTAG PA.

00:26:40.850 --> 00:26:44.133
In that period, it is unchanging.

00:26:45.100 --> 00:26:48.790
It must replicate itself exactly.

00:26:48.790 --> 00:26:53.370
It must clone itself year after year until it matures.

00:26:53.370 --> 00:26:55.420
So it is unchanging, that is RTAG PA.

00:26:55.420 --> 00:26:58.150
For a functional entity, this is impossible.

00:26:58.150 --> 00:27:02.390
There is no functional entity in the universe that is unchanging, not

00:27:02.390 --> 00:27:05.830
even for a minute, let alone twelve lifetimes.

00:27:05.830 --> 00:27:07.510
This is impossible.

00:27:07.510 --> 00:27:10.410
This is Nagarjuna.

00:27:10.410 --> 00:27:13.250
"Can we cancel the first possibility, that is, that

00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:16.671
it stays in your consciousness without changing?"

00:27:17.890 --> 00:27:19.600
Yes, it must change.

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:20.990
If it is a functional entity, it will change.

00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:22.130
Why?

00:27:22.130 --> 00:27:23.810
Because it is driven by a cause

00:27:23.810 --> 00:27:28.470
, that energy begins to slow down over time.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:34.630
Now, Geshe-sensei, are you saying that

00:27:34.630 --> 00:27:38.385
the longer karma stays in your consciousness, the
less powerful it becomes?

00:27:39.395 --> 00:27:40.800
[Student laughter]

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:43.056
Okay, here's another option:

00:27:43.056 --> 00:27:45.206
GAL TE 'GAGS NA 'GAGS GYUR PA'I

00:27:45.206 --> 00:27:46.972
JI LTAR 'BRAS BU SKYE PAR 'GYUR,

00:27:46.972 --> 00:27:50.730
If you say it doesn't change, then it stops.

00:27:50.730 --> 00:27:54.563
Then we don't have to experience the consequences of karma, yay!

00:27:57.312 --> 00:28:02.130
Is it copying or stopping?

00:28:02.130 --> 00:28:04.670
It cannot be replicated, because if it were,
it would remain unchanged.

00:28:04.670 --> 00:28:06.770
And it is a functional entity;

00:28:06.770 --> 00:28:08.090
it cannot stop,

00:28:08.090 --> 00:28:10.410
otherwise all the laws of karma would be broken.

00:28:10.410 --> 00:28:13.170
If it stops, all the laws of karma will be broken, and

00:28:13.170 --> 00:28:14.565
you could do whatever you want.

00:28:14.565 --> 00:28:18.250
Hopefully, karma will stop before it opens,

00:28:18.250 --> 00:28:19.083
okay?  Have

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:23.133
you ever thought about it?

00:28:24.050 --> 00:28:28.242
Okay, can anyone tell me
why the next picture is related?

00:28:33.190 --> 00:28:36.324
Have you ever applied for a job in New York or Los Angeles?

00:28:36.324 --> 00:28:37.474
I'm asking... [laughter]

00:28:39.230 --> 00:28:41.833
You'll be waiting in the waiting room for many hours, right?

00:28:41.833 --> 00:28:45.418
Are you the one who went into the waiting room?  What

00:28:45.418 --> 00:28:47.767
I mean is, for me,
562
00:28:47,767 --&gt; 00:28:50,220a,
your karma is like walking into a waiting room
and finally someone says, "

00:28:50.220 --> 00:28:51.757
Okay, I'll interview you."

00:28:51.757 --> 00:28:53.235
You know what they always say?

00:28:53.235 --> 00:28:55.935
They say, "Oh, it's five o'clock now.
Can you come back tomorrow?"

00:28:55.935 --> 00:28:57.361
You say, "I'll be there at three o'clock."

00:28:57.361 --> 00:28:58.953
They say, "Yes, but..."

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:04.780
That's what it's like to apply for a job in New York or Los Angeles
, right?

00:29:04.780 --> 00:29:06.601
Okay, you know. Okay,

